        "raw_sha256": "a9bc657fb926368561ab2657dfbfbf6a7a0ba5b8c2122f8d1fb8510a0a975262",
        "mathtext": "We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure\n$\\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ on $\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ , where\n$V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})$ satisfies, for $0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta$ ,\n\n$\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,.$\n\n(1.1)\n\nThe main result of this paper is the following.\n",
        "disposition": "NODE",
        "classification": "selected-source-node",
        "reason": "Standing potential/carrier assumptions; source main theorem after this paragraph is not selected.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
