      {
        "id": "S2.SS1.p1",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 514,
        "end_line": 567,
        "raw_sha256": "a71193f93ff747f7278162bc819e4d19d48c177c6640b8132d8cf3c83257317e",
        "mathtext": "We first recall the usual Bouncy Particle Sampler (BPS) for readers\nunfamiliar with the construction [5]. It is a\npiecewise-deterministic Markov process on phase space\n$(x,p)\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\times\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ , where $p$ denotes velocity (equivalently,\nmomentum for unit mass). Its invariant distribution is\n$\\mu\\otimes\\varphi$ , where $\\varphi=\\mathcal{N}(0,I)$ . Between events, the\nparticle moves along a straight line with constant $p$ :\n\n$\\dot{x}_{t}=p_{t}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\dot{p}_{t}=0\\,.$\n\n(2.1)\n\nAt state $(x,p)$ , a bounce occurs at rate\n\n$\\lambda_{\\rm BPS}(x,p)\\coloneqq[p^{\\top}\\nabla V(x)]_{+}\\,.$\n\n(2.2)\n\nEquivalently, conditional on the current state and in the absence of a\nvelocity refresh, the next bounce time $\\tau_{\\rm b}$ satisfies\n\n$\\mathbb{P}(\\tau_{\\rm b}>t\\mid x,p)=\\exp\\Bigl\\{-\\int_{0}^{t}[p^{\\top}\\nabla V(x+sp)]_{+}\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\Bigr\\}\\,.$\n\n(2.3)\n\nAt a bounce, the position is unchanged and the velocity is specularly\nreflected against the gradient. For non-zero $h\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ , set\n\n$R_{h}\\coloneqq I-2\\,\\frac{hh^{\\top}}{\\|h\\|^{2}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptR_{0}\\coloneqq I\\,.$\n\n(2.4)\n\nThe bounce update is $p\\leftarrow R_{\\nabla V(x)}p$ . It preserves\n$\\|p\\|$ , leaves the component tangent to a level set unchanged, and\nreverses the normal component, since\n$(R_{h}p)^{\\top}h=-p^{\\top}h$ . Thus, the particle travels freely\nwhile moving down the potential and bounces, at a rate equal to its\ninstantaneous uphill directional derivative, when it moves up the\npotential. Proximal BPS reuses this bounce mechanism, applied to a localized\nconditional target; the construction is given in Section 3.\n",
        "disposition": "NODE",
        "classification": "selected-source-node",
        "reason": "Only Euclidean phase space, specular reflection and norm preservation are selected; vanilla BPS dynamics/laws/citation remain context.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
