      {
        "id": "S2.SS1.p2",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 568,
        "end_line": 590,
        "raw_sha256": "a0d16f3f3375940ecc2fe9ceaad00dc01e027f4f520e084889260f50045f54c8",
        "mathtext": "The standard bouncy particle sampler also uses independent velocity refreshes to ensure ergodicity, at which $p$ is redrawn from $\\varphi$ . Writing\n\n$(\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}f)(x,p)\\coloneqq\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x,p^{\\prime})\\,\\varphi(\\mathrm{d}p^{\\prime})\\,,$\n\nthe full generator of BPS is\n\n$\\begin{split}(\\mathsf{L}_{\\rm BPS}f)(x,p)&=p^{\\top}\\nabla_{x}f(x,p)+[p^{\\top}\\nabla V(x)]_{+}\\{f(x,R_{\\nabla V(x)}p)-f(x,p)\\}+\\gamma(\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}f-f)(x,p)\\,.\\end{split}$\n\n(2.5)\n\nFor every refresh rate $\\gamma\\geq 0$ , the process with\ngenerator (2.5) leaves\n$\\mu\\otimes\\varphi$ invariant [5], and its position\nmarginal is the desired target $\\mu$ .\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted.",
