        "raw_sha256": "0c1b18fda4177251701514d1fd2f3156c7ce3ac5bd495062e40f905192609329",
        "mathtext": "The joint law (2.6) has the following properties.\n\n(i)\n\nFor every $y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ , the conditional law\n$\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}$ has potential (that is, negative\nlog-density up to an additive constant)\n\n$V_{y}(x)\\coloneqq V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\,.$\n\n(2.9)\n\nThis conditional potential satisfies\n\n$(\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V_{y}(x)\\preceq(\\beta+\\eta^{-1})I\\,,$\n\n(2.10)\n\nso its condition number is at most\n$(1+\\beta\\eta)/(1+\\alpha\\eta)\\leq 2$ . Consequently, for every\nsmooth $f$ ,\n\n$\\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(f)\\leq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}\\|\\nabla f\\|^{2}\\,,$\n\n(2.11)\n\nand\n\n$\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\preceq\\mathrm{Cov}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(X)\\preceq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\,.$\n\n(2.12)\n\n(ii)\n\nThe $Y$ -marginal potential satisfies\n\n$\\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}U_{\\eta}(y)\\preceq\\frac{\\beta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\,.$\n\n(2.13)\n\n(iii)\n\nThe state-space reflection\n\n$\\mathsf{U}:(x,y)\\mapsto(x,2x-y)$\n\n(2.14)\n\npreserves $\\pi_{\\eta}$ and is an involution.\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
