      {
        "id": "S2.SS2.p3",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 745,
        "end_line": 755,
        "raw_sha256": "58e5d7ac5357b94a4d47e1ad10d2b84b7aa83994136af3d043a4cf02368e8e4c",
        "mathtext": "The Hessian\nbound in part (i) follows immediately from (1.1); the\nPoincaré and covariance bounds then follow from the standard\nlog-concavity facts (D.6) and\nLemma D.3 in Appendix D, applied with\n$m=\\alpha+\\eta^{-1}$ and $L=\\beta+\\eta^{-1}$ . The\nmarginal curvature bound in part (ii) is derived in\nAppendix D, at (D.10). The\nreflection statement follows directly from (2.6).\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "S2.SS2.p4",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 756,
        "end_line": 776,
        "raw_sha256": "eddde75c9ed6bb575a0efdf35bff69a410a120aa2329ebb82ab2ea2d05443b8a",
        "mathtext": "We use the standard proximal map convention of\nMoreau [24]:\n\n$\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\coloneqq\\arg\\min_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}\\Bigl\\{V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,.$\n\n(2.15)\n\nThe minimizer is unique under (1.1). The objective\nminimized here is exactly the conditional potential\n(2.9), so $\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)$ is the\nmode of $\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}$ ; the conditional draw is in this\nsense a stochastic analogue of a proximal step, whence the\nterminology arises. This exact minimizer is used below only in the analysis; the implementable algorithm never evaluates it and\ndoes not assume access to a proximal oracle.\nWe use the following\nconditional sampling primitive, introduced in [17].\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "S2.E15",
        "tag": "table",
        "class": "ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table",
        "start_line": 759,
        "end_line": 766,
        "raw_sha256": "6598bffc2f5ea1496c1b4308ed80f591895ec0ed56ec5ac3a6270863f24cc46d",
        "mathtext": "$\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\coloneqq\\arg\\min_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}\\Bigl\\{V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,.$\n\n(2.15)\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted.",
