        "raw_sha256": "bba0ffac57788de5021cebb92fcf309a81d38afd72b0615f0e9573f0cde85905",
        "mathtext": "For probability measures $P\\ll Q$ and $s>1$ , define the Rényi\ndivergence11\n1\n\nOur notation $D_{s}(P\\|Q)$\ncorresponds to $\\mathcal{R}_{s}(P\\|Q)$ in [11, Definition 2.2.23], with the same definition\nand normalization; we use $D_{s}$ here to avoid possible confusion with the reflection operator $R_{h}$ defined in (2.4). of order $s$ and the $\\chi^{2}$ -divergence by\n\n$D_{s}(P\\|Q)\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{s-1}\\log\\int\\Bigl(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}P}{\\mathrm{d}Q}\\Bigr)^{s}\\,\\mathrm{d}Q\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\chi^{2}(P\\|Q)\\coloneqq e^{D_{2}(P\\|Q)}-1\\,.$\n\n(2.16)\n\nWe set $D_{s}(P\\|Q)=+\\infty$ when $P\\not\\ll Q$ . We refer to a\nbound $D_{2}(P\\|Q)\\leq\\Delta$ as an order-2 Rényi\nwarm start bound. Our convention for total variation is\n$\\operatorname{TV}(P,Q)\\coloneqq\\sup_{A}|P(A)-Q(A)|$ .\nWe use the standard inequality\n\n$\\operatorname{TV}(P,Q)\\leq\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\chi^{2}(P\\|Q)}\\,.$\n\n(2.17)\n\nFor any coupling $(X,Y)$ of $P$ and $Q$ ,\n$\\operatorname{TV}(P,Q)\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\{X\\neq Y\\}$ , and a maximal coupling of $X$ and $Y$ attains\nequality.\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Retained §2 context outside the selected reflection/scale/notation background: vanilla process, refresh/thinning, Gibbs/geometric/oracle/divergence results are not admitted.",
