        "mathtext": "If $X_{0}\\sim\\mu_{0}$ and, conditionally on $X_{0}$ ,\n$Y_{0}\\sim\\mathcal{N}(X_{0},\\eta I)$ , then, whenever $\\mu_{0}\\ll\\mu$ ,\n\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}\\mathcal{L}(X_{0},Y_{0})}{\\mathrm{d}\\pi_{\\eta}}(x,y)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}\\mu_{0}}{\\mathrm{d}\\mu}(x)\\,.$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$D_{2}\\bigl(\\mathcal{L}(X_{0},Y_{0})\\|\\pi_{\\eta}\\bigr)=D_{2}(\\mu_{0}\\|\\mu)\\,.$\n\n(2.18)\n\nThe identity also holds in the extended sense when\n$\\mu_{0}\\not\\ll\\mu$ , in which case both sides are infinite.\n",
