      {
        "id": "S3.SS2.p1",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 1394,
        "end_line": 1422,
        "raw_sha256": "231155afacf713e4210585e0f10bcb321c02a55ce710d2b0b23bea696bbbc136",
        "mathtext": "Fix $Y=y$ . Recall from (2.8) that the position\n$X$ to be sampled has conditional law\n\n$\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto e^{-V_{y}(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptV_{y}(x)\\coloneqq V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\,.$\n\nWe construct the half-turn process so that its induced transition\npreserves this law. The\nconstruction starts from vanilla BPS for the conditional target, absorbs\nthe quadratic coupling potential into the deterministic motion, and then\nintroduces\nan independent conditional reference point to localize the remaining\nbounce rate. We begin by introducing a Gaussian momentum\n$p\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)$ . The phase space law to be preserved is\n\n$\\nu_{\\eta,y}(\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}p)\\coloneqq\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\,\\mathcal{N}(0,I)(\\mathrm{d}p)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V_{y}(x)-\\frac{\\|p\\|^{2}}{2}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}p\\,.$\n\n(3.1)\n\nRecall from (2.4) that $R_{h}$ denotes specular\nreflection across the hyperplane orthogonal to $h$ .\n",
        "disposition": "NODE",
        "classification": "selected-source-node",
        "reason": "Conditional target and phase-space measure are contextual identity only; invariance and random-law construction remain OPEN.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "explicit-context-OPEN",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Conditional/stationary target laws are identity context only; no distribution or invariance is proved by this finite target."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "S3.Ex5",
