      },
      {
        "id": "S3.SS2.p2",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 1423,
        "end_line": 1445,
        "raw_sha256": "ffd097dfb59378e4717bfedc5a0da83632c21da134444322d4a0e4e57ed9017e",
        "mathtext": "A natural first attempt is to apply vanilla BPS directly to this\nconditional distribution. Its infinitesimal generator acts on a smooth\ntest function $f$ as\n\n$\\begin{split}(\\mathsf{L}_{y}^{\\rm vanilla}f)(x,p)&=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p^{\\top}\\nabla_{x}f(x,p)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,[p^{\\top}\\nabla V_{y}(x)]_{+}\\bigl\\{f(x,R_{\\nabla V_{y}(x)}p)-f(x,p)\\bigr\\}\\,.\\end{split}$\n\n(3.2)\n\nThe common factor $\\sqrt{\\eta}$ only fixes the unit of time; it does not\nchange the invariant law. We choose this unit so that the harmonic motion\nintroduced below has period $2\\pi$ .\nThe first term gives straight-line motion, while the second reflects the\nmomentum against the full conditional gradient. This process is exact,\nbut it can be expensive: even when $V=0$ , the quadratic coupling potential\n$\\|{\\cdot}-y\\|^{2}/(2\\eta)$ produces a stationary mean bounce rate of order\n$\\sqrt{d}$ .\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Generator/vanilla/boomerang motivational context; not needed to prove the concrete finite recurrence or its estimates.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Generator/vanilla/boomerang motivational context; not needed to prove the concrete finite recurrence or its estimates."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "S3.E2",
        "tag": "table",
        "class": "ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table",
        "start_line": 1427,
        "end_line": 1436,
        "raw_sha256": "16eefe4107464ce10d9fa97d56b7cf4a7a64bb6716bf3175a817e7c44d6ae50f",
        "mathtext": "$\\begin{split}(\\mathsf{L}_{y}^{\\rm vanilla}f)(x,p)&=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p^{\\top}\\nabla_{x}f(x,p)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,[p^{\\top}\\nabla V_{y}(x)]_{+}\\bigl\\{f(x,R_{\\nabla V_{y}(x)}p)-f(x,p)\\bigr\\}\\,.\\end{split}$\n\n(3.2)\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Generator/vanilla/boomerang motivational context; not needed to prove the concrete finite recurrence or its estimates.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Generator/vanilla/boomerang motivational context; not needed to prove the concrete finite recurrence or its estimates."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "S3.SS2.p3",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 1446,
        "end_line": 1468,
        "raw_sha256": "620d2e2d4742bcad7d3ab4adc7ce696424fef1df0595184aa6ddea1f67636ef9",
        "mathtext": "To reduce the number of bounce events, we put the quadratic part of the\nconditional gradient into the deterministic dynamics. This gives the\ngenerator\n\n$\\begin{split}(\\mathsf{L}_{y}^{\\rm harm}f)(x,p)&=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p^{\\top}\\nabla_{x}f(x,p)-\\frac{(x-y)^{\\top}}{\\sqrt{\\eta}}\\nabla_{p}f(x,p)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,[p^{\\top}\\nabla V(x)]_{+}\\bigl\\{f(x,R_{\\nabla V(x)}p)-f(x,p)\\bigr\\}\\,.\\end{split}$\n\n(3.3)\n\nThe first line is the Hamiltonian flow associated with the quadratic\ncoupling potential: between bounces, it rotates $(x-y)/\\sqrt{\\eta}$ and\n$p$ . This use of a quadratic reference flow, with the remaining force\nhandled by bounce events, is analogous to the Boomerang\nsampler [4].\nThe direct harmonic generator (3.3)\nstill bounces against the full gradient $\\nabla V$ , so its bounce rate\ncan remain large.\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Generator/vanilla/boomerang motivational context; not needed to prove the concrete finite recurrence or its estimates.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Generator/vanilla/boomerang motivational context; not needed to prove the concrete finite recurrence or its estimates."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "S3.E3",
        "tag": "table",
        "class": "ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table",
        "start_line": 1450,
        "end_line": 1459,
        "raw_sha256": "d99e605e49381534943c978b0bbfd452b4e16329bb6bac6dae589727ab8c14ce",
        "mathtext": "$\\begin{split}(\\mathsf{L}_{y}^{\\rm harm}f)(x,p)&=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p^{\\top}\\nabla_{x}f(x,p)-\\frac{(x-y)^{\\top}}{\\sqrt{\\eta}}\\nabla_{p}f(x,p)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,[p^{\\top}\\nabla V(x)]_{+}\\bigl\\{f(x,R_{\\nabla V(x)}p)-f(x,p)\\bigr\\}\\,.\\end{split}$\n\n(3.3)\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Generator/vanilla/boomerang motivational context; not needed to prove the concrete finite recurrence or its estimates.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
