        "mathtext": "For every fixed $y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ and initial phase space point\n$(x_{0},p_{0})$ , the event-driven dynamics in Algorithm 1, with\nthe reference point fixed at $\\widetilde{x}$ , defines a unique\nnon-explosive, time-homogeneous Markov process. The phase space measure\n$\\nu_{\\eta,y}$ is stationary for this process. In particular, the\nreturned position $x_{\\pi}$ is well-defined almost surely.\n",
        "disposition": "NODE",
