      {
        "id": "S3.Thmtheorem2",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition",
        "start_line": 1658,
        "end_line": 1667,
        "raw_sha256": "7ea671a0133070f8519837db910ebd94ab02c86e479f5f8ad5cddf761b651b3c",
        "mathtext": "Proposition 3.2 (Reversibility of the conditional half-turn kernel).\n\nFor every $y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ , let $\\mathcal{H}_{y}$ be the Markov kernel on\n$\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ induced by Algorithm 1; thus\n$\\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\\cdot)$ is the law of the returned position $x_{\\pi}$\nfor input $(x,y)$ . Then $\\mathcal{H}_{y}$ is reversible with respect to\n$\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}$ .\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Half-turn kernel reversibility is outside this finite-recursion delta and remains OPEN.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
