        "mathtext": "For every $y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ , let $\\mathcal{H}_{y}$ be the Markov kernel on\n$\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ induced by Algorithm 1; thus\n$\\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\\cdot)$ is the law of the returned position $x_{\\pi}$\nfor input $(x,y)$ . Then $\\mathcal{H}_{y}$ is reversible with respect to\n$\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}$ .\n",
