      {
        "id": "S3.Thmtheorem3",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition",
        "start_line": 1675,
        "end_line": 1693,
        "raw_sha256": "84967a73394015e3b8976bab5d7ff67169417218ca431cb1ed0b3e1340e503ca",
        "mathtext": "Proposition 3.3 (Stationary bounce count).\n\nThere exists a universal constant $K_{\\rm id}\\geq 1$ such that the\nfollowing holds. Suppose that $(x_{0},Y)\\sim\\pi_{\\eta}$ . Conditional on\n$Y$ , let $\\widetilde{X}\\sim\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y}$ be independent of\n$x_{0}$ , and let $p_{0}\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)$ be independent of all position\nvariables. If $N_{\\rm b}^{\\rm id}$ denotes the number of bounce events\nin the resulting ideal half-turn process of Algorithm 1, then\n\n$\\mathbb{E}N_{\\rm b}^{\\rm id}\\leq K_{\\rm id}\\beta\\eta\\sqrt{d}\\,.$\n\n(3.10)\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Stationary bounce count/expected cost is outside this finite-recursion delta and remains OPEN.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Stationary bounce count/expected cost is outside this finite-recursion delta and remains OPEN."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "S3.Thmtheorem3.p1",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 1677,
