        "raw_sha256": "717157e13a704f73f9a21f1563bdf86b0a2b4ea0182d280e2da752e8b137f679",
        "mathtext": "Fix $y,\\widetilde{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$ . In the notation of\n(3.4), the bounce rate\n(3.9) reads\n\n$\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)=\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,[p^{\\top}h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)]_{+}\\,.$\n\nThe deterministic harmonic flow, namely the solution\n(4.5) of (3.8), and\nthe bounce map are\n\n$\\displaystyle\\Phi_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)$\n$\\displaystyle\\coloneqq\\bigl(c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}+(x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\cos t+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p\\sin t,\\;-\\eta^{-1/2}(x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})\\sin t+p\\cos t\\bigr)\\,,$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)$\n$\\displaystyle\\coloneqq(x,R_{h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)}p)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptR_{0}\\coloneqq I\\,.$\n\nThe bounce map is an involution. Although there is a possible discontinuity at $h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)=0$ , this creates no ambiguity\nbecause the event rate vanishes there.\n",
        "disposition": "NODE",
        "classification": "selected-source-node",
        "reason": "Exact fixed-reference λ, Φ, S, involution, zero-normal convention and possible discontinuity.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
