      {
        "id": "A1.SS1.p2",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 2889,
        "end_line": 2912,
        "raw_sha256": "deaf05e75397a7778841acf49396c564e53e7e90553b45f3bad8e16493d19f73",
        "mathtext": "Let $(E_{n})_{n\\geq 1}$ be independent $\\operatorname{Exp}(1)$\nrandom variables. Starting from\n$\\zeta_{0}\\coloneqq(x_{0},p_{0})$ at time $T_{0}\\coloneqq 0$ , define recursively\n\n$\\displaystyle S_{n+1}$\n$\\displaystyle\\coloneqq\\inf\\Bigl\\{u\\geq 0:\\int_{0}^{u}\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(\\Phi_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}}))\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\geq E_{n+1}\\Bigr\\}\\,,$\n\n(A.1)\n\n$\\displaystyle T_{n+1}$\n$\\displaystyle\\coloneqq T_{n}+S_{n+1}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\zeta_{T_{n+1}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}\\bigl(\\Phi_{S_{n+1}}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}})\\bigr)\\,,$\n\n(A.2)\n\nwhen $S_{n+1}<\\infty$ . If the set is empty, set\n$T_{n+1}=S_{n+1}=\\infty$ and stop the recursion. Between jumps, set\n$\\zeta_{T_{n}+t}=\\Phi_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}})$ for\n$0\\leq t<S_{n+1}$ .\n",
        "disposition": "NODE",
        "classification": "selected-source-node",
        "reason": "Finite recursion is selected; iid Exp law remains a full-process source input not claimed here. Includes finite/∞ split and arcs.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
