      {
        "id": "A1.SS1.p3",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 2913,
        "end_line": 2974,
        "raw_sha256": "831b561c07be5a0b17321aea9f6333e77431dde0b0165a1fd60c8cda9fa883f6",
        "mathtext": "To prove non-explosion, define the shifted harmonic energy\n\n$H_{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl\\{\\eta^{-1}\\,\\|x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\|^{2}+\\|p\\|^{2}\\bigr\\}\\,.$\n\nThe flow and each bounce preserve this energy. Hence, with\n$\\mathcal{E}\\coloneqq H_{y,\\widetilde{x}}(x_{0},p_{0})$ , every state produced by\nthe recursion satisfies\n\n$\\|p\\|\\leq\\sqrt{2\\mathcal{E}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\|\\leq\\sqrt{2\\eta\\mathcal{E}}\\,.$\n\nBecause $\\nabla V$ is $\\beta$ -Lipschitz,\n$\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\\leq\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})$ throughout the path, where\n\n$\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})\\coloneqq\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\beta\\sqrt{2\\mathcal{E}}\\,\\bigl\\{\\sqrt{2\\eta\\mathcal{E}}+\\|c_{y,\\widetilde{x}}-\\widetilde{x}\\|\\bigr\\}\\,.$\n\nHence,\n\n$\\int_{0}^{u}\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(\\Phi_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}(\\zeta_{T_{n}}))\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\leq\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})\\,u\\,.$\n\nIf $\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})=0$ , the event rate\nvanishes and there are no jumps. Otherwise,\n(A.1) implies, for every finite waiting time,\n\n$S_{n+1}\\geq\\frac{E_{n+1}}{\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})}\\,.$\n\nIf the recursion does not terminate, it follows that\n\n$T_{n}\\geq\\frac{\\sum_{j=1}^{n}E_{j}}{\\bar{\\lambda}_{\\mathcal{E}}(y,\\widetilde{x})}\\longrightarrow\\infty$\n\nalmost surely by the strong law of large numbers. Thus, the jump times\ncannot accumulate, and the recursive construction defines a unique\nprocess for all $t\\geq 0$ . Finally, the\nmemoryless property of the exponential clocks gives the time-homogeneous\nMarkov property. This is precisely the integrated hazard construction\nof Davis [12, Section 2].\n∎\n",
        "disposition": "NODE",
        "classification": "selected-source-node",
        "reason": "Energy/envelope/waiting finite estimates selected; SLLN/divergence/global process/Markov/Davis theorem are OPEN and separately inventoried.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "covered-finite-estimates-future-OPEN",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [
