        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 2976,
        "end_line": 2998,
        "raw_sha256": "e5f9ff0b95e97353aca5f0bb168e4a16cc82003ee14799f01013f9b6b307d698",
        "mathtext": "With the process now constructed, we prove the stationarity assertion in\nProposition 3.1 and record the stronger operator facts used\nto analyze the averaged kernel. Recall $\\nu_{\\eta,y}$ from\n(3.1), and define momentum\nreversal by\n\n$\\mathsf{R}(x,p)\\coloneqq(x,-p)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt(\\mathsf{R}F)(x,p)\\coloneqq F(\\mathsf{R}(x,p))\\,.$\n\nAs usual, we use the same symbol for $\\nu_{\\eta,y}$ and its Lebesgue\ndensity:\n\n$\\nu_{\\eta,y}(x,p)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V_{y}(x)-\\frac{\\|p\\|^{2}}{2}\\Bigr\\}\\,.$\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
