      {
        "id": "A1.Thmtheorem1",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition",
        "start_line": 2999,
        "end_line": 3032,
        "raw_sha256": "3269de741ad5699e64f84a19d513af8eed4a8954d933331ef4b1aec0186b430e",
        "mathtext": "Proposition A.1 (Path reversal, invariance, and the $L^{2}$ semigroup).\n\nLet $(\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}})_{t\\geq 0}$ be the Markov transition\noperators of the process constructed in\nProposition 3.1. For every $t\\geq 0$ ,\n\n$(\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}})^{*}=\\mathsf{R}\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\mathsf{R}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{on }L^{2}(\\nu_{\\eta,y})\\,.$\n\n(A.3)\n\nConsequently:\n\n(i)\n\n$\\nu_{\\eta,y}$ is invariant;\n\n(ii)\n\n$(\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}})_{t\\geq 0}$ is a strongly continuous\ncontraction semigroup on $L^{2}(\\nu_{\\eta,y})$ ;\n\n(iii)\n\nif $\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}:L^{2}(\\nu_{\\eta,y})\\to L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y})$ denotes Gaussian momentum averaging, then\n$\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}^{*}$ is a\nself-adjoint Markov contraction on $L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y})$ .\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Later A.1 stationarity/reversal/trajectory-law/semigroup argument, outside the selected finite-recursion delta; retained RAW, no admission.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
        "compiled76_projection": {
          "status": "EXCLUDED_OPEN_OR_CONTEXT",
          "current_BODY_or_definition_lines": [],
          "compiled_parent_regions": [],
          "reason": "Later A.1 stationarity/reversal/trajectory-law/semigroup argument, outside the selected finite-recursion delta; retained RAW, no admission."
        }
      },
      {
