        "raw_sha256": "c026dfb3aaa0aa43f7a8f3d382c66fcf729d399495ff9b58c1cd1d31b40f7571",
        "mathtext": "The identity (A.3) is a\nmomentum-reversed form of detailed balance. To see the mechanism\nformally, write\n$\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{x}}=\\mathcal{A}+\\mathcal{J}$ , where\n\n$\\displaystyle\\mathcal{A}f(x,p)$\n$\\displaystyle\\coloneqq\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p^{\\top}\\nabla_{x}f(x,p)-\\frac{(x-c_{y,\\widetilde{x}})^{\\top}}{\\sqrt{\\eta}}\\nabla_{p}f(x,p),$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\mathcal{J}f(x,p)$\n$\\displaystyle\\coloneqq\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\\bigl\\{f(\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p))-f(x,p)\\bigr\\}.$\n\nMomentum reversal reverses the harmonic flow, so\n$\\mathsf{R}\\mathcal{A}\\mathsf{R}=-\\mathcal{A}$ . Moreover,\n\n$\\mathcal{A}\\log\\nu_{\\eta,y}(x,p)=-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,p^{\\top}h_{\\widetilde{x}}(x)=-\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,p)+\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}(x,-p).$\n\nFormal integration by parts gives\n\n$\\mathcal{A}^{*}=-\\mathcal{A}+\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}-\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}\\circ\\mathsf{R}.$\n\nThe bounce map $\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}$ is a\n$\\nu_{\\eta,y}$ -preserving involution, commutes with $\\mathsf{R}$ , and\nsatisfies $\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}\\circ\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}=\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}\\circ\\mathsf{R}$ . A formal change of variables\ntherefore gives\n\n$\\mathcal{J}^{*}G=(\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}\\circ\\mathsf{R})(G\\circ\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}})-\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}G.$\n\nCombining the two identities yields\n\n$\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{x}}^{*}G=-\\mathcal{A}G+(\\lambda_{\\widetilde{x}}\\circ\\mathsf{R})(G\\circ\\mathsf{S}_{\\widetilde{x}}-G)=(\\mathsf{R}\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\mathsf{R})G.$\n\nFormally exponentiating this identity gives\n$(\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}})^{*}=\\mathsf{R}\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\mathsf{R}$ ; Gaussian momentum averaging\nthen removes $\\mathsf{R}$ and produces an ordinary self-adjoint position\nkernel.\n",
