      {
        "id": "A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7",
        "tag": "div",
        "class": "ltx_para",
        "start_line": 3245,
        "end_line": 3260,
        "raw_sha256": "55183b1a41376e42621e5637a37323604a6c20223d49bf713c7f6538a07f3e29",
        "mathtext": "Finally, Gaussian momentum averaging satisfies\n$\\mathsf{R}\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}^{*}$ and\n$\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}\\mathsf{R}=\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}$ . Combining these identities with\n(A.3) gives\n\n$(\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}^{*})^{*}=\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}(\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}})^{*}\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}\\mathsf{R}\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\mathsf{R}\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}\\mathsf{\\Pi}_{p}^{*}\\,.$\n\nThis proves self-adjointness; the Markov and contraction properties are\ninherited from $\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{x}}$ .\n∎\n",
        "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
        "classification": "excluded-with-reason",
        "reason": "Later A.1 stationarity/reversal/trajectory-law/semigroup argument, outside the selected finite-recursion delta; retained RAW, no admission.",
        "overlap_policy": "Nested paragraph/theorem/display records overlap intentionally; coverage is by source region, not a theorem-count metric.",
